# Python bytecode cache (from graph/build_graph.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Oversized raster exports — render on demand from graph.dot / build_graph.py
graph/*.png

# Graphviz cleanup intermediate (created+deleted on each render; never commit)
graph/graph

# Rendered SVG: regenerable, and NOT byte-stable -- fdp in Graphviz 15 relays the
# graph out on every run even with a fixed seed and byte-identical input, so it
# rewrote ~12k lines (1.1 MB) per commit carrying no information. The tracked,
# byte-stable artifacts are graph.dot and graph.html; render the SVG on demand:
#   python graph/build_graph.py    (or: dot -Kfdp -Tsvg graph/graph.dot -o graph/graph.svg)
graph/graph.svg
